WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/charging/components/charging-list/EfficiencyPanel.tsx — a PURE presentational leaf its
  parent renders only when `computeEfficiencyStats(...)` returns non-null `EfficiencyStats`:
    GlassPanel(p-5) → h3.section-title[ Activity icon (text-neon-green)
                                        + t('charging.efficiency.title','Charging Efficiency')
                                        + hint span: t('…hint','Wall-to-battery energy conversion')
                                                     ({stats.count} t('…sessionsWithData','sessions with data')) ]
                    → grid-cols-1 sm:2 lg:4 of four inner GlassPanel(p-5 text-center):
                        1 Average Efficiency : fmtPercent(avgEfficiency) [cyan-300] + bar width min(avg,100)%
                        2 Best Session       : fmtPercent(best.efficiency) [emerald-300] + formatDateTime(best.date)
                        3 Worst Session      : fmtPercent(worst.efficiency) [rose-300]  + formatDateTime(worst.date)
                        4 Wall-to-Battery Loss: fmtWithUnit(wallLoss,'kWh') [amber-300]
                                                + `${fmtNumber(totalUsed)} kWh → ${fmtNumber(totalAdded)} kWh`
  Formatters (web defaults, lib/numberFormat.ts): _globalPrecision=2, _globalLocale='en-US';
  fmtPercent = fmtNumber(v,2)+'%'; fmtWithUnit = fmtNumber(v,2)+' '+unit; safeNumber → non-finite ⇒ 0.
  formatDateTime (lib/dateFormat.ts): localized date+time, '—' on nil/invalid.
  No data hooks live in the leaf (the prompt's "Data sources" is just `useTranslation`); the loading / empty /
  error / stale / offline branches are the Apple HIG states contract layered over the single web rendering.

